.TH PHONE-WEBCAM 1 "October 2026" "phone-webcam" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phone-webcam \- use an Android phone's camera as a webcam
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phone-webcam
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
[\fB\-\-simulate\-missing\fR \fIKEYS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phone-webcam
turns the camera of an Android phone, connected over USB, into a virtual webcam
that other applications can use. It runs scrcpy to read the camera, turns the
picture as asked, and writes it to a v4l2loopback device. The picture can be
rotated, mirrored and previewed while it is running, and the camera, frame
rate and bitrate can be changed without interrupting the webcam.
.PP
When it starts, it checks that everything it needs is installed and tells you
what is missing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Run every dependency check, print the result and exit, without opening a
window.
.TP
.BI \-\-simulate\-missing " KEYS"
Pretend that the named checks fail, to preview how a missing tool is shown.
.I KEYS
is a comma separated list of check names.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/phone-webcam/prefs.json
The saved orientation, stream settings and side panel width.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
With \fB\-\-check\fR, a required dependency is missing.
.TP
.B 2
The graphical stack is incomplete, so no window can be opened.
.TP
.B 3
The window could not be opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scrcpy (1),
.BR adb (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
